The conditions in this Section apply only when you redistribute the Software, in source or binary form, or distribute a Derivative Work. They do not apply to private use of the Software.

If you redistribute the Software or distribute a Derivative Work, you must:

(a) include the above copyright notice, this license, and the disclaimer in Section 8 with every copy of the Software or substantial portion of it. For source distributions, this means in the source files or in a NOTICE, README, or documentation file distributed with them. For binary or compiled distributions, this means in the documentation distributed with the product;

(b) if you distribute the Software or a Derivative Work as part of a product with a user interface, display a credit line naming "Nythxion Studios" as the original copyright holder, in a credits, about, or settings screen that is accessible from the product's main menu, without requiring any hidden gesture, secret input, or timed action. The credit must be at least as legible as the surrounding interface text and may read, for example: "Developed by Nythxion Studios (NSAAL 1.0)." If the product has no user interface, the credit line must instead appear in its README or documentation; and

(c) in modified files, include a notice stating that the files have been changed.

1A. Substantial Modification Required for Distribution

You may not redistribute the Software, in source or binary form, or distribute a Derivative Work, unless it has been substantially modified. A modification is substantial only if it adds, removes, or changes the functionality of the Software. Incorporating the Software into another product or service is a substantial modification, provided that the product or service adds substantial functionality beyond the Software itself. Wrapping the Software in a product that adds no substantial functionality of its own, such as a splash screen, menu, or launcher, is not a substantial modification. Cosmetic changes, renaming, formatting, configuration, and packaging changes are not substantial modifications. Redistributing the Software unmodified, or with only minor modifications, is not permitted, except that this restriction does not apply to a product or service that is a substantial modification under this Section. This Section does not restrict private use of the Software.

